From 016488017567bfe455b718df7df5868665ba305c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:10:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] host pool: full-coverage default (MOE_HOST_POOL_FRAC=100)
 + per-table sizing from routing concentration (MOE_HOST_POOL_SIZING=1)

Two changes, both from the measured pool baseline (wip/host-pool-speed, 1 x R9700, 122B-A10B, -ncmoe 48,
5258-token prompt + 2000-token decode, arms alternating, ~163/~53/~13 MiB of demand disk read per decode
token at FRAC 50/80/100):

1. FULL COVERAGE BY DEFAULT.  The pool's decode cost is dominated by the experts it does not hold: decode
   17.76 t/s at FRAC 80 (the old default) vs 20.59 at FRAC 100 against 22.34 pinned, with the disk reads
   falling 165 -> 100 GiB per run.  Over half of the -20.5 % gap was that uncovered fraction.  The
   MOE_HOST_POOL_RAM_PCT ceiling still clamps the pinned total to 85 % of MemAvailable whatever FRAC asks
   for, so a box the set does not fit in is unchanged -- and at full coverage the pool pins exactly what the
   pinned master would, so the remaining gap is the mode's own overhead (the number this makes visible).

2. PER-TABLE SIZING BY CONCENTRATION (opt-in, MOE_HOST_POOL_SIZING=1).  MOE_HOST_POOL_FRAC gives every host
   table the same slot count, so the pinned bytes go to a table with a long cold tail exactly as to one with
   a flat hot set.  A table's TOTAL routed mass cannot discriminate -- a top-k router hands every table
   n_used experts per token, so it is a constant, and sizing by heat mass reproduces the uniform rule
   exactly -- but its CONCENTRATION can: cov_t = the slots it needs to hold MOE_HOST_POOL_COV_PCT of its own
   prior mass, fitted to the same total byte budget (one-shot, at the first pool build, when every host
   tensor is registered, so it stays order-independent).  Offline on the reference trace at FRAC 80 this
   takes the disk tier from 48.7 to 28.5 MiB per decode token with h unchanged
   (wip/host-pool-speed/tools/pool-sizing-sim.py, HANDOVER section 4/F6).  Default stays uniform until gated.

Also updates the two help/log texts that named the old 80 % default.
